MULTI-REFERENCE POSE TRANSFER — generate a single photographic image.

• POSE SOURCE — [IMG_1]
${sourceInstr}

TRANSFER LEVEL — ${transferLabel.toUpperCase()}:
${transferInstr}

• HERO IDENTITY & PROPORTIONS — [IMG_2]   ? ABSOLUTE PRIORITY
[IMG_2] is a reference for a practical puppet/figurine character. Photograph this exact figurine — with its exact proportions, head size, limb thickness, body shape — as-is in a real location. Do not apply realistic human anatomy. This is NOT a human, it is a sculpted character with intentional non-realistic proportions.

Do NOT inherit [IMG_2]'s clean studio lighting or render quality — the final character is re-photographed in the light and lens of the final scene${decorOn ? ' (i.e. [IMG_3])' : (bgMode === 'cyc') ? ` (i.e. ${cycColor.name} cyclorama studio)` : ''}.

The pose from [IMG_1] adapts to this figurine's anatomy — never the reverse.${decorBlock}

DIRECTIVE: Render [IMG_2] performing the pose of [IMG_1]${decorOn ? ' with [IMG_3] used only as visual style' : (bgMode === 'cyc') ? ` on a ${cycColor.name} (${cycColor.hex}) studio cyclorama` : ''}, using the framing and 3D orientation specified by the TRANSFER LEVEL. Pose, framing, camera, and 3D body orientation come from [IMG_1].${decorOn ? ' Grade, grain, contrast, and light mood come from [IMG_3] without copying its place.' : ''}${subjectLine}${matLine}${techLine}${physicsLine}

OUTPUT: Photoreal, in-camera footage. No CG look. Single frame. ${decorOn ? 'A real photograph with [IMG_1] setup, [IMG_2] identity, and [IMG_3] style only.' : (bgMode === 'cyc') ? 'Clean studio commercial photography aesthetic.' : 'Seamless integration.'}
